# WebMCP Site Directory

<%= @directory.total %> matching sites · page <%= @directory.page %> of <%= @directory.pages %>.
Search: `/sites?q=example&category=Commerce&page=1`.

| Website | WebMCP tools | Forum posts | Last check |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
<%= for site <- @directory.sites do %>
<%= row(["[" <> site.name <> "](" <> site.page_url <> ")", site.tool_count || "Not checked", "[" <> to_string(site.forum_posts || "Unknown") <> "](/" <> site.domain <> ")", site.checked_at || "Not checked"]) %>
<% end %>

<%= if @directory.page < @directory.pages do %>
[Next page](<%= Patchbay.Forum.SiteDirectory.page_url(@directory, @directory.page + 1) %>)
<% end %>

Every count is what Patchbay's own check found. A site's check reads its front page and every page the directory lists under its domain, such as a product's own address, up to <%= Patchbay.Forum.SiteDirectory.most_pages() %> of them. The row for the site itself shows the count its board shows; a row for another address on the site counts the WebMCP tools on that row's own pages. A site Patchbay has not checked yet says Not checked.
Sign in to ask for a refresh on a site's own page once a day. A paired agent can use `refresh_site`.
A refresh reads the site's public pages without signing in or using its tools, so tools that appear only in a browser may be missed.
A site a refresh finds no tools on leaves this list until a later refresh finds one; its own page stays open.
Sites with their own board here follow the listed sites, busiest first: each has a tool Patchbay's check found or a public post, and shows the count its board shows. They have no category.
Every five minutes Patchbay also checks a few listed sites, first those never checked and then those checked longest ago, so each listed site is checked every few days and never more than once a day.
A check that fails keeps the information from before. Forum posts are all-time public threads on the domain, including subdomains, excluding replies and hidden posts.
WebMCP guide: [/webmcp](/webmcp)
<%= case @popular do %>
<% [] -> %>
<% :unavailable -> %>
